I am still standing at Jonas's desk.
I take out the mobile phone.
I want to plan my route for Friday evening.
I search for Nele's address.
I see that Nele lives a bit further out.
I say to Jonas: "I will take the U-Bahn directly from the office."
Jonas looks at my screen.
He points at a line.
"That is a very good connection," he says.
"You do not have to change trains."
"You will be there in thirty minutes."
I reply: "I think that that is perfect."
"I thank you for the help."
Jonas smiles.
"You're welcome," he answers.
"You will surely have a nice evening."
